  (text "DUAL ACTIVE BRIDGE   48 V Mako pack  <->  400 V link,  3 kW,  single phase shift\n\nT1 is the planar transformer, n = 8.33. Its windings and their mutual coupling live in\nxfmr.lib, attached to T1 by Sim.Library = ${KIPRJMOD}/xfmr.lib, and KiCad resolves that\nitself into an absolute .include when it builds the netlist.\n\nThat indirection is not decoration. K is a DEVICE line in SPICE, not a dot command, and\nthe GUI simulator prepends a dot to any schematic text directive that lacks one - so a\nbare \"K1 L1 L2 0.9999\" on the sheet reaches ngspice as \".k1 ...\" and the circuit will not\nparse. A relative \".include\" does not work either, because KiCad drives ngspice as a\nshared library and hands it the netlist in memory, with no file for a relative path to\nresolve against. Sim.Library avoids both: KiCad does the resolving.\n\nL3 = 56 uH is the customer-supplied series inductance on the HIGH-voltage side, and with\nthe turns ratio and the frequency it is what sets power transfer:\n\n        P = V1 * (V2/n) * phi * (pi - phi) / (2 * pi^2 * f * L)\n\nf = 100 kHz.  phi = 54 deg, set by delaying VG3 and VG4 by 1.5 us of the 10 us period.\n85 kHz wants 41.9 deg; above about 119 kHz this transformer cannot reach 3 kW at all.\n\nD1-D8 are the body diodes and the model is WRONG without them: with no freewheel path the\n100 ns dead time chops the inductor current and the transfer falls from 3.0 kW to 1.2 kW.\n\nOnly the four gate nets G1-G4 are labels. Every power connection is drawn as a wire.\n\nSimulated 3005 W in, 2938 W out, 97.8%.   Closed form 3001 W.   Agreement 0.1%."
    (at 35 255 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom))
    (uuid "e6164dfb-703e-491a-8d7a-9e7901f5efb9")
  )
